{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if a man seduces.</b> After finishing the discussion of theft of property, he began to discuss theft of the heart — that is, the seducer." "<b>Who is not betrothed.</b> This implies that if she is betrothed, he is liable to stoning." "<b>He shall surely pay a bride-price to him.</b> Against his will, so that no other man may humiliate her if he takes her and recalls her disgrace — for she was a young girl and did not know to guard herself against his seduction. But he may divorce her with a get, since she consented to him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:46.271539837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}